  "Question": "No common point of line \\(l\\) and circle \\(O\\) is known. To prove that \\(l\\) is tangent to circle \\(O\\), the usual approach is to",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Draw a perpendicular to \\(l\\) through the center \\(O\\), and prove that the length of the perpendicular segment equals the radius",
    "B": "Join \\(O\\) to any point on \\(l\\), and prove that the resulting segment is perpendicular to \\(l\\)",
    "C": "Prove that \\(l\\) passes through the center \\(O\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
